The generator executes the original four optimization methods with their full
random schedules and assertions, capturing inputs at the operations under test.
No trial loop is shortened. The identified prebuilt helper is used without
recompilation. The fixture binds source, generator, frontend and helper hashes.
Rust expectations for contraction, overlap and pullback use direct exhaustive
path/coordinate evaluation, independent of the production elimination kernels.
Inverse columns also compare with the exact original native result; zero free
coordinates and the matrix product are checked separately.

Rust uses typed packed bits and unsigned seeds. The invalid RHS value 2 and
negative seed are rejected by packed-vector/unsigned conversion. Callback tables
are owned: replacement constructs an immutable instrument with the same version.
These substitutions do not claim Python object identity or Python RNG identity.
